 報名/票券: https://forms.gle/jPeqBkywysHrXzAt7\n\nJoin us for an engag
 ing discussion with Prime Minister of the Republic of Estonia Kristen Mich
 al on:\n\nEstonia at the Front Line: Security\, Resilience\, and Technolog
 y: Security\, Europe\, and Technology\n\nEstonia sits at the intersection 
 of some of the defining challenges of our time. Bordering Russia and on NA
 TO’s eastern flank\, Estonia has had to make security and resilience a n
 ational priority. At the same time\, it has emerged as one of the world’
 s most digitally advanced societies. For Estonia\, security\, agility and 
 innovation are not abstract ideas -- they are necessities.\n\nIn this conv
 ersation with Estonian Prime Minister Kristen Michal\, we will explore wha
 t it means to lead a country on NATO’s eastern flank at a time of profou
 nd geopolitical change\; why the outcome of Russia’s war against Ukraine
  will shape Europe and the wider world\; and how Europe can take greater r
 esponsibility for its own security.\n\nWe will also discuss Estonia’s re
 markable evolution into one of the world’s most advanced digital societi
 es\, its ambitions in artificial intelligence\, and what smaller countries
  can teach us about adapting when new technologies are reshaping economies
 \, governments and societies.\n\n\nThe discussion will be moderated by Mic
 hael McFaul\, Ken Olivier and Angela Nomellini Professor of International 
 Studies\, Senior Fellow at the Hoover Institution\, at the Freeman Spogli 
 Institute for International Studies and at the Woods Institute for the Env
 ironment.\n\nKristen Michal has served as 
